<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vijaya (Champa)</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Đồ Bàn</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vijaya was a region and capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/champa">Champa</a> in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/binh-dinh-province">Bình Định province</a>, central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>. From around the 11th century it was the chief royal centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cham">Cham</a> kings, with the citadel of Đồ Bàn and many brick towers. The Vietnamese emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-thanh-tong">Lê Thánh Tông</a> captured and sacked it in 1471, breaking Champa's power, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tay-son-dynasty">Tây Sơn</a> later made the area their base.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vijaya-champa.jpg" alt="Vijaya (Champa)" width="320" height="452" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: sailko · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vietnam,_shiva,_da_thap_banh_it_(torre_d%27argento),_stile_di_transiz._tra_my_son_A1_e_thap_mam,_Xi-Xii_sec,_01.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
